extraction_notes: "Printed 118-119. EXPERIENCE: the `Nightbane Sorceror & Nightbane Mystic` ladder, printed 233, read off a render (class-renders/nb-nightbane-sorcerer-mystic-ladder-crop.png), stored as the lower bound of each band; stated on this O.C.C. and not on the Nightbane R.C.C. per survey D2. RACE: restricted to `nb-nightbane` (survey D2); that R.C.C. is not yet imported. Not supersedes_race: ability 7 says the character keeps all the natural powers of the Nightbane R.C.C., so this is training, not a transformation. SPELLS: the lists are nb-sorcerer''s, unchanged - `level1`..`level4` from the Nightbane invocation index and `invocations` the 131 names the chapter describes (see nb-sorcerer''s notes for every spelling resolved and for Summon Entity, which has no row). Printed 118-119 says `three spells from each magic level one to four, for a total of twelve spells (two from each)`: three from each makes the twelve the same sentence states and two from each makes eight, so three is stored. The spell gained each level is `equal to his own level`, stored as one pick from the list capped at the character''s level (BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT F61), as nb-sorcerer does. Learning or buying further spells at any time is prose. SAVES: `+3 to save vs magic` is stored as spell_magic only, as nb-sorcerer stores its +4; +2 vs horror factor and +2 vs possession as printed. The human Sorcerer''s +2 vs mind control is not printed for this O.C.C. and is not stored. P.P.E.: printed 119 says it is `the same as that of all members of his race: 3D6x10+20 plus the P.E. attribute. Add 2D6+6 per level of experience`. Stored as printed. The Nightbane R.C.C. itself prints P.E. plus 3D6x10+20, +3D6 per level (printed 88), so the two printings disagree on the per-level gain; which one a paired character receives is for the R.C.C. import to settle, and is not decided here. TALENTS: one at first level, none free thereafter, more bought with permanent P.P.E. This replaces the R.C.C.''s free progression rather than adding to it, so it is the `Nightbane Talents (Sorcerer)` ability, prose only; no talents block. MORPHUS/FACADE: the hand to hand bought with related picks affects the Facade only and the Morphus fights at roughly martial arts - prose on the Physical category and in restrictions. SKILLS: Read/Write/Speak Native Language is split into the speaking and literacy rows, both 98%. Research is 50% in this book (printed 57), so +20% is 70. Computer Operation +10% on the catalog''s 40 is 50; Mathematics: Basic +25% on 45 is 70. The two Lore picks offer the six Lore skills on Nightbane''s own list (printed 48), as nb-sorcerer does. Rogue and Military are None. Secondary skills are `from those listed`, stored as the related categories without their bonuses. MONEY: 3D4x100+200 cash, stored; 2D4x1,000 in property is not cash and is in restrictions. EQUIPMENT: `Varies. Most sorcerers own a small occult library, a personal computer, and other useful items` - the library and computer cite the rows nb-sorcerer cites; `other useful items` is not stored. HIT POINTS AND S.D.C. are not printed on the entry; they are the Nightbane R.C.C.''s (printed 88) and printed 36''s 3D6 S.D.C."
