## Lore

Nightbane Sorcerers are a very rare breed: ordinary Nightbane who have been
trained in the mystic arts, usually at the hands of a human sorcerer. About half
were apprentices who never realized their supernatural nature until their
Becoming. The rest were discovered by sorcerers who decided to teach them magic.
Some ancient Nightbane in the Underground Railroad are sorcerers, and now and
then pass their knowledge on to worthy students.

It is a difficult path. The demands of learning magic often conflict with the
visualization a Nightbane needs to develop Talents, so these sorcerers end up
somewhat less effective at either specialty than a dedicated human sorcerer or
a normal Nightbane. On the other hand, they can draw on both sources of power at
will.

## GM Notes

**Talents and spells.** A Nightbane Sorcerer receives a single free Talent at
first level and no more. Further Talents cost permanent P.P.E., which is also
the energy the sorcerer casts with - every Talent bought is spell power given
up.

**Facade and Morphus.** The hand to hand skill a Nightbane Sorcerer buys with
related skill picks applies to the Facade only. In Morphus form the character
has natural combat powers roughly equivalent to martial arts.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-nightbane-sorcerer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-nightbane-sorcerer';

